---
source: crates/togi/tests/read/status.rs
expression: text(&ran.stdout)
---
Show the session at a glance

The activity (the open night with its start, elapsed observed time and the task it runs, the day, a stop or a dead end); session and BIOS context; then one table row per tuning unit with its physical cores, applied D, hard ceiling C, remaining D-C, hold hours and climbing/held/finished state. Tagged U retains observed-failure or censored write-limit witnesses. Statistical S is diagnostic and never authorizes a step. Day policy shows experimental hold + exact night qualification, applied/read-back versus proposed and paused-saved profiles, machine allowance and every classified event, finish/held reasons and current exact profile daily evidence under the 95% fixed-rate model. A Night part shows elapsed observed time, queue shares, mapping, outstanding qualification and reproductions. Status shows policy facts; it computes no ceiling or eligibility itself. A defect names its recorded decisions and the `togi reset --all` that starts fresh. After daily observations exist, a Day section lists boots, checkpointed hours per read-back profile, clean/unclean ends and the last unclean boot's reset reason. Each unclean end of a day-observed boot becomes a question until answered: what togi saw, the four answers and the `togi day answer` command that records each; an answered one shows the current answer. Read-only, rendered from the journal. A different ruleset warns before rendering; a different schema is refused.

An event of a kind this build does not know is skipped and an unknown field is ignored; stderr says which, after the output.

Usage: togi status [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --state-dir <path>
          State directory
          
          [default: /var/lib/togi]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  togi status                     The session in the default state directory
  togi --state-dir <dir> status   The session in <dir>, such as a copied state directory
